//! A reflexivity whose endpoint calls a definition that omits its implicits.
//!
//! The checker solves such implicits from the types of the arguments, and it
//! fills the declared type with the solutions. The kernel replays the relation
//! that the checker decides at each endpoint of the filled type.
//!
//! `stepImplicit` takes the carrier and the three points as implicits. A call
//! writes only the two paths. `twoLevels` states a reflexivity one level up,
//! so its endpoints hold that call. The checker forms the filled type again,
//! and each reflexivity carries its dialogues to the kernel.
//!
//! - see: #5521
//! - see: `omitted-carrier-in-body.gandr` — a composite whose carrier the signature solves

/// A composite of two paths, its carrier and its points implicit.
def stepImplicit[t : Type, a : t, b : t, c : t](
  p : Path[.A = t](a, b),
  q : Path[.A = t](b, c)
) -> Path[.A = t](a, c) =
  Path.walk (fun (y) { type(Path[.A = t](a, y)) }) q p

/// The composite of `f` with a reflexivity, related to `f` one level up.
def twoLevels(
  A : Type,
  x : A,
  y : A,
  f : Path[.A = A](x, y)
) -> Path[.A = Path[.A = Path[.A = A](x, y)](stepImplicit f (Path.here y), f)](
  Path.here (stepImplicit f (Path.here y)),
  Path.here f
) =
  Path.here (Path.here f)
